# TypeScript Rules

## Project Context
- **TypeScript**: v5.9.3 (strict mode enabled)
- **Runtime validation**: Zod v4.3.5 for schema validation and type inference
- **Type safety enhancement**: `@total-typescript/ts-reset` configured globally
- **Module system**: ESM with bundler/Node resolution depending on target
- **Monorepo structure**: Shared packages via `@repo/*` with explicit subpath exports

For detailed module system architecture, see @apps/docs/content/docs/architecture/esm-strategy.mdx

## Core Principles

### Type Declarations
- **Prefer interfaces over types** for object shapes
- **Use `type` for**: unions, utility types, mapped types, Zod inference
- **Avoid enums**; use const objects or union types
- **Infer types when possible**; only declare when reusing across functions/components

### Naming Conventions
- **Variables**: camelCase with auxiliary verbs for booleans (`isLoading`, `hasError`, `canEdit`)
- **Directories**: lowercase-with-dashes (`components/auth-wizard`, `lib/error-handling`)
- **Exports**: prefer named exports (exception: Next.js pages/layouts require default)

### Function Patterns
- **Use RORO** (receive object, return object) for multiple parameters
  - ✅ `const createUser = ({ name, email }: CreateUserInput) => ({ id, name, email })`
  - ❌ `const createUser = (name: string, email: string) => [id, name, email]`
- **Prefer functional patterns**; avoid classes and decorators (exception: framework requirements)
  - ✅ `const double = (x: number) => x * 2`
  - ❌ `class MathUtil { double(x: number) { return x * 2 } }`

### Code Style
- **Single-line conditionals** without braces for simple cases
  - ✅ `if (!value) return null`
  - ❌ `if (!value) { return null }`
- **Single-line arrow functions** without braces
  - ✅ `const double = (x: number) => x * 2`
  - ❌ `const double = (x: number) => { return x * 2 }`
- **Early returns** for guard clauses; avoid unnecessary `else`
  - ✅ `if (!user) return null; return <Profile user={user} />`
  - ❌ `if (!user) { return null } else { return <Profile user={user} /> }`

## Imports & Module Organization

### Type-Only Imports
- Use `import type` for type-only imports to ensure they're erased at runtime

### Shared Packages
All shared packages use **subpath exports** for better tree-shaking. See @apps/docs/content/docs/architecture/packages.mdx for complete package reference.

**Key packages:**
- **`@repo/utils/*`**: Async, web3, logger, debug utilities (always use subpaths)
- **`@repo/error/*`**: Platform-specific error handling (node/nextjs/browser/react)
- **`@repo/core`**: API client and types (generated from OpenAPI)
- **`@repo/react`**: React hooks and TanStack Query integration
- **`@repo/ui/components/*`**: Shared UI components (Shadcn/ui based)

Examples:
  - ✅ `import { delay } from "@repo/utils/async"`
  - ✅ `import { captureError } from "@repo/error/nextjs"` (Next.js apps)
  - ✅ `import { captureError } from "@repo/error/node"` (Fastify apps)
  - ❌ `import { delay } from "@repo/utils"` (no root export)

### Lodash Usage
- Use `lodash-es` with per-function imports for tree-shaking and RSC compatibility
  - ✅ `import isEmpty from "lodash-es/isEmpty"`
  - ❌ `import { isEmpty } from "lodash-es"` (breaks tree-shaking)

## Type Safety Model

### Zod-First Validation
- Validate untrusted data at runtime boundaries (API routes, form inputs, external APIs)
- Use Zod schemas for both validation and type inference
  - ✅ `const userSchema = z.object({ name: z.string(), email: z.email() })`
  - ✅ `type User = z.infer<typeof userSchema>`
- **Schema location**: colocate with feature; only centralize when genuinely reused
  - ✅ `app/api/users/schema.ts` (feature-specific)
  - ❌ `lib/schemas/index.ts` (premature centralization)

### Disabled TS ESLint Rules
The following "unsafe" rules are disabled globally to support Zod-first validation: `no-unsafe-assignment`, `no-unsafe-call`, `no-unsafe-member-access`, `no-unsafe-return`, `no-unsafe-argument`. This allows inferred types internally while maintaining runtime safety at boundaries.

### ts-reset Enhancements
`@total-typescript/ts-reset` is configured globally via `tools/typescript/reset.d.ts`, providing:
- Better array method types (`filter`, `includes`, etc.)
- Stricter `JSON.parse` return type
- Improved `fetch` response types

## Architecture Safety

### Explicit Return Types
- Exported functions and API handlers must declare explicit return types
  - ✅ `export const getUser = async (id: string): Promise<User | null> => {}`
  - ❌ `export const getUser = async (id: string) => {}` (implicit return type)

### Validation Functions
- Functions that validate must return result objects, never throw
  - ✅ `const validate = (input: unknown): { valid: boolean; error?: string } => {}`
  - ❌ `const validate = (input: unknown) => { if (!isValid) throw new Error() }`

## Framework-Specific Rules

### Next.js
- `app/**/page.tsx` and `app/**/layout.tsx` require default exports
- Use React Server Components by default; mark client components with `"use client"`

### Fastify
- Fully functional patterns; no classes or decorators
- Use Fastify's type-safe route definitions with schemas

## Error Handling
- Use guard clauses with early returns
- Place happy path last for readability
- **Error utilities**: Use `@repo/error` with platform-specific imports
- See @.cursor/rules/base/error-handling.mdc for full error handling patterns

